WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.461 --> 00:00:16.142
man was Roger Redbeard!

2
00:00:16.162 --> 00:00:20.343
"W-what do you mean, you'll make us walk the plank?"

3
00:00:20.964 --> 00:00:22.284
Maggie asked nervously.

4
00:00:23.265 --> 00:00:24.465
Roger Redbeard grinned.

5
00:00:24.485 --> 00:00:27.506
"I'm just joking around, kids," he said.

6
00:00:27.526 --> 00:00:30.067
"I like to practice my pirate voice.

7
00:00:32.392 --> 00:00:33.812
Aargh!" Henry glanced at his friends.

8
00:00:35.013 --> 00:00:37.293
He could tell they were thinking the same thing he was.

9
00:00:38.214 --> 00:00:39.694
Had Roger taken their tickets?

10
00:00:39.714 --> 00:00:41.835
"Excuse me, Mr.

11
00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:43.175
Redbeard," he said.

12
00:00:43.195 --> 00:00:45.476
"Can we ask you a question?"

13
00:00:45.496 --> 00:00:49.737
"Sure." Roger took a sip from the plastic cup he was holding.

14
00:00:49.757 --> 00:00:51.457
"Is it about pirates?"

15
00:00:52.938 --> 00:00:53.898
"Not exactly."

16
00:00:54.358 --> 00:00:55.399
Henry cleared his throat.

17
00:00:55.419 --> 00:01:00.360
"We're just wondering where you've been since the last time we saw you."

18
00:01:01.308 --> 00:01:02.508
Roger looked surprised.

19
00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:04.849
"I walked downtown to get lunch."

20
00:01:05.769 --> 00:01:08.230
Henry noticed that Roger was holding a plastic cup.

21
00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:12.231
It had a logo printed on it that said SCGS.

22
00:01:12.251 --> 00:01:14.052
"Why do you ask?"

23
00:01:14.072 --> 00:01:16.052
"No reason."

24
00:01:16.832 --> 00:01:18.693
Henry traded another look with his friends.

25
00:01:18.713 --> 00:01:22.834
"Um, did you see anyone else on the beach while you were walking?"

26
00:01:23.714 --> 00:01:24.535
Roger shrugged.

27
00:01:24.555 --> 00:01:27.135
"It's pretty quiet at this end of town.

28
00:01:27.916 --> 00:01:29.136
It's mostly private land.

29
00:01:29.792 --> 00:01:32.374
The only person I passed out here was the Jones girl."

30
00:01:32.394 --> 00:01:34.215
"The Jones girl?"

31
00:01:34.535 --> 00:01:35.116
Maggie said.

32
00:01:35.136 --> 00:01:36.337
"Who's that?"

33
00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:40.379
"Sorry, I don't remember her first name," Roger said.

34
00:01:40.399 --> 00:01:43.141
"But her parents own the general store in town."

35
00:01:44.042 --> 00:01:46.564
Henry realized Roger must be talking about Anna.

36
00:01:46.584 --> 00:01:48.165
"Did she see you?"

37
00:01:48.505 --> 00:01:49.406
he asked Roger.

38
00:01:49.426 --> 00:01:51.947
"I doubt it," Roger replied.

39
00:01:51.967 --> 00:01:53.909
"She was running through the surf."

40
00:01:54.729 --> 00:01:56.170
He took another sip of his drink.

41
00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.492
"Is that all you want to know?

42
00:01:59.244 --> 00:02:02.425
Because if you don't have any questions about pirates, I'd better move along."

43
00:02:02.445 --> 00:02:05.266
"Okay. Bye," Henry said.

44
00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:10.067
Roger wandered away, disappearing soon behind some rocks.

45
00:02:12.148 --> 00:02:13.748
Maggie checked to make sure he was gone.

46
00:02:13.768 --> 00:02:16.029
"Do you think he's telling the truth?"

47
00:02:16.509 --> 00:02:17.049
she asked.

48
00:02:18.389 --> 00:02:22.490
"He wasn't carrying that cup when we saw him before," Henry reminded her.

49
00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:25.571
"So he probably is telling the truth."

50
00:02:25.591 --> 00:02:29.396
"That means he couldn't have stolen our tickets," Cole said.

51
00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:32.438
"Not necessarily," Maggie argued.

52
00:02:32.458 --> 00:02:34.579
"How far away is the town?

53
00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.641
It might only take five minutes to walk there.

54
00:02:38.481 --> 00:02:39.902
We should ask William or Anna."

55
00:02:41.283 --> 00:02:44.064
"Speaking of Anna, shouldn't she be a suspect?"

56
00:02:44.404 --> 00:02:45.065
Henry asked.

57
00:02:45.085 --> 00:02:48.166
"Roger said he saw her running down the beach.

58
00:02:48.907 --> 00:02:50.328
That's kind of suspicious."

59
00:02:50.348 --> 00:02:52.849
"Not really," Maggie said.

60
00:02:52.869 --> 00:02:55.951
"She was looking for booty, just like the rest of us."

61
00:02:57.531 --> 00:02:58.212
Henry nodded.

62
00:02:58.956 --> 00:03:01.977
"But she was alone, while the rest of us had partners.

63
00:03:03.017 --> 00:03:06.038
And she knew exactly where all the tide pools were.

64
00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:10.819
What if she grabbed the tickets before Luke and Nathan reached the tide pool?"

65
00:03:11.079 --> 00:03:11.619
he asked.

66
00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:13.340
Maggie gasped.

67
00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:14.880
"You could be right!

68
00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:18.661
Nathan said he and Luke had trouble finding their tide pool."

69
00:03:18.681 --> 00:03:21.702
"But why would she want the tickets?"

70
00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:22.942
Cole wondered.

71
00:03:22.962 --> 00:03:25.343
"She's not even interested in pirates."

72
00:03:26.363 --> 00:03:27.083
"That's true."

73
00:03:27.884 --> 00:03:28.804
Henry thought back.

74
00:03:29.692 --> 00:03:31.534
"She said the legends were stupid."

75
00:03:32.455 --> 00:03:33.696
Just then they heard a shout.

76
00:03:34.417 --> 00:03:35.578
Luke was running toward them.

77
00:03:35.598 --> 00:03:37.459
"What is it?"

78
00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:38.560
Maggie called.

79
00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.402
"Did you find the booty?"

80
00:03:40.422 --> 00:03:43.625
"Maybe," Luke replied breathlessly.

81
00:03:43.645 --> 00:03:46.267
"We didn't find anything at the marina.

82
00:03:47.328 --> 00:03:50.451
I told the others I'd run and see if you guys found anything.

83
00:03:51.292 --> 00:03:53.974
But on the way here, I noticed something interesting.

84
00:03:54.835 --> 00:03:55.336
Come on!"

85
00:03:58.956 --> 00:04:00.257
He led the way back to the bay.

86
00:04:06.141 --> 00:04:08.582
A rowboat was bobbing in the water just offshore.

87
00:04:09.383 --> 00:04:11.964
A skull-and-crossbones flag was flying from it.

88
00:04:11.984 --> 00:04:14.326
"That's a pirate flag!"

89
00:04:14.626 --> 00:04:15.566
Cole exclaimed.

90
00:04:15.587 --> 00:04:17.448
"You guys pull in the boat.

91
00:04:17.908 --> 00:04:18.889
I'll run and get the others."

92
00:04:21.330 --> 00:04:24.072
The rowboat was tied to a small dock with strong rope.

93
00:04:25.696 --> 00:04:28.837
Henry, Maggie, and Luke pulled on the rope as Cole ran off.

94
00:04:32.239 --> 00:04:36.461
By the time Cole returned with Nathan, William, and Anna, the boat was on the beach.

95
00:04:40.062 --> 00:04:41.523
"There's a pirate chest on board!"

96
00:04:41.823 --> 00:04:42.463
Luke called.

97
00:04:44.004 --> 00:04:46.225
Cole helped Luke lift the chest out of the boat.

98
00:04:47.966 --> 00:04:48.986
Then Henry opened it.

99
00:04:49.006 --> 00:04:52.448
"Wow!" he cried when he saw what was inside.

100
00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.522
"Handheld video game players!

101
00:04:56.322 --> 00:04:59.084
There are seven of them, one for each of us!"

102
00:04:59.104 --> 00:05:01.506
"Are you kidding?"

103
00:05:01.926 --> 00:05:02.786
Maggie exclaimed.

104
00:05:02.807 --> 00:05:04.428
"Let me see!"

105
00:05:06.629 --> 00:05:08.530
She grabbed one of the players and turned it on.

106
00:05:09.311 --> 00:05:11.492
A picture of a pirate ship appeared on the screen.

107
00:05:11.512 --> 00:05:14.915
"Whoa!" Luke peered over Maggie's shoulder.

108
00:05:14.935 --> 00:05:18.978
"It's already loaded with the Revenge of the Pirate's Ghost game!"

109
00:05:18.998 --> 00:05:21.019
"No way!"

110
00:05:21.499 --> 00:05:22.200
Nathan yelled.

111
00:05:23.352 --> 00:05:24.092
"Can I have one?"

112
00:05:24.332 --> 00:05:25.033
Cole asked.

113
00:05:25.933 --> 00:05:27.714
The kids each grabbed one of the players.

114
00:05:29.355 --> 00:05:30.715
Anna was the last to take one.

115
00:05:30.735 --> 00:05:36.478
"I've been dying to get one of these," she said slowly.

116
00:05:36.498 --> 00:05:42.240
"My parents said they're too expensive, but I've been saving my allowance all summer."

117
00:05:43.101 --> 00:05:44.641
That made Henry stop and think.

118
00:05:45.462 --> 00:05:47.362
"You're right, Anna," Henry said.

119
00:05:47.382 --> 00:05:54.713
"These game players are expensive, a lot more expensive than a bunch of movie tickets, even for a

120
00:05:54.753 --> 00:05:56.796
premiere." "Yeah."

121
00:05:57.777 --> 00:06:00.160
Nathan sounded distracted as he played with his game.

122
00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:01.662
"So what?"

123
00:06:02.624 --> 00:06:03.405
Henry shrugged.

124
00:06:04.286 --> 00:06:08.472
"So why would someone steal the tickets, but not this booty?"
